; A line that begins with '^' ends the file that contains it: an
; undocumented maintainer aid for bisecting a journal.  In an included
; file it ends only that file, and parsing resumes in the including file
; after the include line; an included file whose first line is '^'
; contributes nothing.  A '^' that does not begin a line is ordinary
; text.  The journal lives in .dat files so the semantic bisimulation,
; whose oracle has no '^' sentinel, does not replay it.

test -f $sourcepath/test/regress/caret-ends-file.dat reg --format '%(payee) [%(tag("Memo"))]\n' Food
Main first []
Included before caret []
Main after include [a^b]
end test
